=3 Notes
* The {m:Qiqirn Pecheur} in this zone all drop a {i:Willow Fishing Rod|Willow Fishing Rod|17391} or a {p:Fly Lure}, but given the time constraint and uncertainty of fishing up the Orobon, it is highly suggested to bring your own rod and lure/bait.
* The goal of this assault is to fish up an Orobon NM and return the item you receive to the NPC at the start.
* Fishing at any point in the map will net one of the following monsters: Orobon, Pugil, Pugil, Crab, Kraken. It all depends on luck

:* It is possible that the first thing you fish at the starting point can be the Orobon (verified, first hand encounter).

* No fishing skill is needed.
* The Orobon will only be fished at a certain point on the map.
* There are 4 NPC fisherman also on the map. At first they will be dismissive toward you. Once you fish up 4 or 5 enemies, they will change text.
* NPC speech will read along the lines of either "this area is no good" or "I've got a good feeling about this area."
** Only one NPC will say they like their area, continue fishing at this NPC.
* After 4 or 5 more enemies fished, the NPC will start giving more specific locations, something along the lines of "to the North is a good spot."
* The Orobon has a fairly large amount of HP, plus usual Orobon moves that can silence, plague, slow, and other nasty debuffs.
* Whomever deals the killing blow will automatically receive the athapot to return to the NPC.

=2 Walkthrough
* Have two or three people fishing at a time, if you can handle it, fish at different NPCs, or have other party members out at other NPCs.
* Once the NPC dialog changes, finding the proper NPC is priority.
* You can fish up the Orobon without NPC text changing. People have been lucky and fished up only after finding the proper NPC, but without details.
* Kill the Orobon

